{
  "id": "m25l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Usar enumeraciones",
    "en": "Using enumerations"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Buscar, recorrer y comparar"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Puedes obtener un miembro a partir de su valor llamando al Enum como una función: `Color(1)` -> `Color.ROJO`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from enum import Enum",
          "",
          "class Color(Enum):",
          "    ROJO = 1",
          "    VERDE = 2",
          "",
          "print(Color(2).name)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "VERDE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Y puedes **recorrer** todos los miembros con un bucle for sobre el Enum."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "for c in Color:",
          "    print(c.name)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "ROJO",
          "VERDE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Compara miembros por identidad (`estado is Estado.ACTIVO`); cada miembro es único."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Look up, iterate and compare"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "You can get a member from its value by calling the Enum like a function: `Color(1)` -> `Color.ROJO`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from enum import Enum",
          "",
          "class Color(Enum):",
          "    ROJO = 1",
          "    VERDE = 2",
          "",
          "print(Color(2).name)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "VERDE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "And you can **iterate** over all members with a for loop on the Enum."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "for c in Color:",
          "    print(c.name)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "ROJO",
          "VERDE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Compare members by identity (`estado is Estado.ACTIVO`); each member is unique."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m25l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define un Enum `Estado` (ACTIVO=1, INACTIVO=0) y una función `nombre_estado(n)` que devuelva el nombre del estado con valor `n`.",
        "en": "Define an Enum `Estado` (ACTIVO=1, INACTIVO=0) and a function `nombre_estado(n)` returning the name of the state with value `n`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from enum import Enum",
        "",
        "# define Estado y nombre_estado(n)"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from enum import Enum",
        "",
        "class Estado(Enum):",
        "    ACTIVO = 1",
        "    INACTIVO = 0",
        "",
        "def nombre_estado(n):",
        "    return Estado(n).name"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Estado(n) te da el miembro; usa .name."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Estado(n) gives the member; use .name."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "nombre_estado",
          "harness": "assert nombre_estado(1) == 'ACTIVO'\nassert nombre_estado(0) == 'INACTIVO'"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m25l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define un Enum `Talla` (S=1, M=2, L=3) y una función `listar()` que devuelva la lista de nombres ['S', 'M', 'L'] recorriendo el Enum.",
        "en": "Define an Enum `Talla` (S=1, M=2, L=3) and a function `listar()` returning the list of names ['S', 'M', 'L'] by iterating the Enum."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from enum import Enum",
        "",
        "# define Talla y listar()"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from enum import Enum",
        "",
        "class Talla(Enum):",
        "    S = 1",
        "    M = 2",
        "    L = 3",
        "",
        "def listar():",
        "    return [t.name for t in Talla]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Recorre el Enum con un for y recoge t.name."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Iterate the Enum with a for and collect t.name."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "listar",
          "harness": "assert listar() == ['S', 'M', 'L']"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}